            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital course of your patient, a 27-year-old female, admitted on 20/11/2025 with acute right lower quadrant abdominal pain, nausea, and low-grade fever. Clinical examination revealed marked tenderness at McBurney's point with rebound tenderness. Laboratory investigations confirmed elevated inflammatory markers. Abdominal ultrasonography supported the diagnosis of acute appendicitis. The patient underwent laparoscopic appendectomy on 21/11/2025 without intraoperative complications. Postoperatively, she received intravenous antibiotics, analgesics, and fluid replacement. Wound healing was satisfactory, vital signs remained stable throughout, and the patient was mobilised early. She was discharged home on 22/11/2025 in good general condition. Please ensure follow-up in approximately two weeks for wound inspection and review of histopathological results. Should any concerns arise, do not hesitate to contact our department.</div>"
            },
